@main
TOS Semaphores

Counting semaphores built on ll/sc atomic instructions.
Threads that cannot acquire a semaphore yield and retry,
spinning through the scheduler rather than busy-waiting.

A semaphore is a single i64 in memory (ll/sc operate on 64-bit values):
  value > 0 — available (value = number of permits)
  value == 0 — all permits taken, waiters must yield and retry
@

  import "services"

  extern atomic_load(addr: *i64) -> i64
  extern atomic_dec_if_positive(addr: *i64) -> i64
  extern atomic_inc(addr: *i64)

@api sem_init(sem, value) — Initialize a semaphore with the given count.

  sem_init(sem: *i64, value: i64)
      *sem = value

@api sem_wait(sem) — Acquire a permit, yielding until one is available.

@tech
Uses atomic_dec_if_positive which atomically reads the value,
and if positive, decrements it and returns 1. If zero, returns 0
without modifying memory. On failure, the thread yields its
timeslice and retries after being rescheduled.
@

  sem_wait(sem: *i64)
      while atomic_dec_if_positive(sem) == 0
          yield()

@api sem_post(sem) — Release a permit (atomically increment the count).

  sem_post(sem: *i64)
      atomic_inc(sem)

@api sem_trywait(sem) -> i64 — Non-blocking acquire. Returns 1 on success, 0 on failure.

  sem_trywait(sem: *i64) -> i64
      atomic_dec_if_positive(sem)
